      "category": "security",
      "title": "I got targeted: Trying to get your credentials via a git post-checkout hook",
      "url": "https://frankwiles.com/posts/i-got-targeted/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/cd5gdk",
      "score": 80,
      "comments": 25,
      "author": "frankwiles",
      "published": "2026-10-02T22:19:02Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Attackers weaponize Git post-checkout hooks to trigger silent arbitrary code execution and exfiltrate SSH keys, environment variables, and tokens.",
        "Attacks often leverage submodules, repo templates, or path traversals to plant executable scripts into the target's local .git/hooks directory.",
        "Mitigate hook abuse by overriding core.hooksPath globally, inspecting untrusted repos before checkout, and monitoring Git credential helper activity."
      ]
